===============================================================================
                             alt-commits Suite
===============================================================================

The alt-commits toolset (alt-lookup, alt-scan, and alt-browser) tracks and
maps cherry picks across the Linux kernel repository.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Python Requirements
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

* Python 3.6+: Required for core tools (`alt-lookup`, `alt-scan`, and the
  CLI mode of `alt-browser`).
* Standard Library: Core tools rely solely on standard modules with no
  external dependencies.
* Textual (Optional): Required for the interactive TUI in `alt-browser`. If it
  is not installed, `alt-browser` falls back to a CLI-only mode.

  Install via pip:
      pip install textual

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Quick Start & Setup
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Set the $LINUX_GIT environment variable to point to your local target Linux
kernel Git repository:

    export LINUX_GIT="/path/to/linux-kernel-repo"

Once $LINUX_GIT is set, all tools (alt-lookup, alt-scan, and alt-browser) will
automatically default to targeting this repository.

NOTE: The very first time you run alt-lookup when no database exists, an
initial automatic scan will process the repository history and will take a
while to complete. If you prefer to generate the initial database explicitly
with visible progress before performing queries, you can run "alt-scan"
first:

    alt-scan

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Main Workflow: Querying Alt Commits with alt-lookup
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

For everyday development, alt-lookup is the primary entry point. You do not
need to manually trigger scanning scripts before running queries; alt-lookup
handles database management behind the scenes.

1. Automatic Database Refresh & Algorithm Upgrades
   When you run alt-lookup, it checks the database (.git/alt-commits.db in the
   kernel-source repository). If the database does not exist or has an outdated
   algorithm version, alt-lookup automatically executes a full rebuild
   ("alt-scan --rebuild --quiet") to regenerate the database from scratch.
   Additionally, if the database has not been modified in the last 7 days,
   alt-lookup automatically executes an incremental scan ("alt-scan --quiet")
   in the background to bring the database up to date before returning your
   results.

   To disable automatic scanning (for instance, on a restricted system or
   during rapid offline queries), pass the --no-scan flag.

2. Common Usage Examples

   * Find all sibling commits (cherry picks) for a SHA:

       alt-lookup e4e9b9248ff

     Returns a list of all matching commit SHAs that belong to the same group
     as e4e9b9248ff.

   * Compare two commit SHAs:

       alt-lookup e4e9b9248ff 1042a0b12c

     Exits with return code 0 if the two SHAs represent equivalent commits
     (belong to the same group) or 1 if they do not. Useful in bash scripts and
     automated patch validation pipelines.

   * Lookup all SHAs in a specific Group ID:

       alt-lookup g1042

     Group IDs must always be prefixed with 'g'.

   * View Database Metrics & Statistics:

       alt-lookup stats

     Displays active detection filters, total linked commits, group size
     distributions, and last checkpoint information.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Detection Algorithm & Matching Logic
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The alt-scan engine scans commit history using a multi-pass detection pipeline.
It groups matching commits into equivalence sets using a Union-Find (Disjoint
Set) data structure based on three prioritized detection ranks:

1. Rank 1: Explicit Cherry-Pick Tags (CHERRY_PICK_TAG)
   - Scans commit message bodies for standard Git cherry-pick annotations:
     "(cherry picked from commit <40-char-sha>)"
   - Performs subject cross-validation by comparing normalized commit subject
     lines (stripping brackets like "[PATCH v2]" or "[stable]").
   - If the referenced commit exists and normalized subject lines match, the
     two SHAs are linked into the same group.

2. Rank 2: Patch Diff Matching (SUBJECT_AND_DIFF)
   - Groups candidate commits sharing normalized subject lines.
   - Computes stable patch IDs using "git patch-id --stable" on candidate diffs.
   - Links commits that share identical code diffs, accurately matching
     patches that were cherry-picked without explicit message tags.

3. Rank 3: Subject & Author Timestamp Matching (SUBJECT_AND_TIMESTAMP)
   - Compares candidate commits that share normalized subject lines.
   - Matches commits with identical author timestamps (author_date).
   - Enforces a maximum cycle gap (75 days / ~1 kernel release window) to ensure
     unrelated commits with generic subjects are not incorrectly merged.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data Architecture & Storage
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Database Storage (alt-commits.db)

   * Location: Stored automatically inside the kernel-source repository's
     Git directory at ".git/alt-commits.db" (for example,
     kernel-source/.git/alt-commits.db).
   * Isolation & Cleanup: Because it lives inside .git/, the database is
     completely untracked by Git, isolates data per kernel-source checkout,
     and survives system reboots.
   * Concurrency & Safety:
     - Uses SQLite Write-Ahead Logging (WAL) mode (PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL;),
       allowing alt-lookup and alt-browser to read from the database
       concurrently while alt-scan writes to it.
     - Uses a process file lock (.git/alt-commits.db.lock via fcntl.flock)
       to prevent multiple alt-scan instances from executing simultaneously.

2. Ignore List Synchronization (alt-commits-ignored.txt)

   The ignore file contains commit SHAs that should be excluded from grouping
   (such as false-positive diff matches or copy-pasted tags).

   * Storage Location: Lives in the version-controlled SUSE kernel tree under
     "scripts/alt-commits/alt-commits-ignored.txt" so that rules can be shared
     across all developers via Git.
   * Fetching from origin/scripts:
     - When alt-lookup, alt-scan, or alt-browser starts, it checks the commit
       timestamp of "scripts/alt-commits/alt-commits-ignored.txt" on the remote
       tracking branch "origin/scripts".
     - If the file on origin/scripts has a newer commit timestamp than the local
       file's modification time on disk, the script loads the newer rules
       directly in-memory without touching your working tree file on disk.
   * Modifying and Persisting Ignore Rules:
     - IMPORTANT: If you are going to modify the alt-commits-ignored.txt file
       (either manually or through alt-browser), you must make sure you have
       it updated to the latest version from the origin/scripts branch before
       making changes.
     - To ignore or un-ignore commits, open the interactive browser via
       alt-browser or use its non-interactive CLI flags.
     - Marking a group or SHA as ignored in alt-browser updates the active
       set in memory and immediately saves the merged list to
       "scripts/alt-commits/alt-commits-ignored.txt".
     - You can then commit and push alt-commits-ignored.txt to origin/scripts
       to share the ignore rules with the rest of the team.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Detailed Tool Reference
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

alt-lookup:
  Query tool for inspecting commit groups, comparing SHAs, and fetching
  metrics.

  Usage: alt-lookup [targets...] [options]

  Arguments:
    targets                SHA(s), Group ID (e.g. 'g1042'), or 'stats'.
                           Pass two SHAs to perform a comparison. Note: Group
                           IDs MUST be prefixed with 'g'.

  Options:
    --db DB_PATH           Custom SQLite DB path (defaults to
                           .git/alt-commits.db in kernel-source repo).
    --ignored FILE_PATH    Custom ignore text file path.
    -t, --types TYPES      Detection type threshold or list:
                           1 = Cherry-Pick Tag
                           2 = Patch Diff (Patch-ID) Match
                           3 = Subject & Timestamp Match (default: 3)
    -g, --group GID        Lookup all hashes for a specific Group ID directly.
    --no-scan              Prevent automatic execution of alt-scan if DB is
                           old/missing.

alt-scan:
  Scanner engine that parses commit ranges, matches patch diffs and
  timestamps, and updates SQLite.

  Usage: alt-scan [repo_path] [options]

  Arguments:
    repo_path              Path to Git repository target (defaults to
                           $LINUX_GIT).

  Options:
    --db DB_PATH           Custom SQLite DB path.
    -j, --jobs JOBS        Number of parallel worker processes to spawn
                           (default: CPU count).
    -v, --verbose          Enable detailed multi-line output.
    -q, --quiet            Suppress all terminal output.
    --rebuild              Force a full rescan from scratch, clearing existing
                           database records.

alt-browser:
  Terminal User Interface (TUI) built with Textual for interactive inspection
  and editing. Automatically falls back to non-interactive CLI mode if Textual
  is not installed.

  Usage: alt-browser [repo_path] [options]

  Arguments:
    repo_path              Path to Git repository target (defaults to
                           $LINUX_GIT).

  Options:
    --db DB_PATH           Custom SQLite DB path.
    --ignored FILE_PATH    Custom ignore text file path.
    -i, --ignore TARGET    Ignore commit SHA(s) or Group ID(s) (e.g. 'g1042').
    -u, --unignore TARGET  Unignore commit SHA(s) or Group ID(s).
    --list-ignored         List all currently ignored SHAs.

  Interactive TUI Keybindings (when Textual is installed):
    q                      Quit application.
    s                      Search by Commit SHA.
    m                      Search by Commit Message text.
    f                      Filter display by Detection Type.
    i                      Toggle Ignore/Unignore status for current SHA or
                           Group (persists to disk).
    I                      Show/Hide ignored items in lists.
    Tab / Shift+Tab        Move focus between Group, SHA, and Diff panes.